Z||000000||Monkeyman||09-24-2000||01:36 PM||||I just installed Windows Millenium over Win98.  Everything seems allright, but somehow I lost my driver for my trackball.  When I had Win98, I could get into the correct mouse window which was specific to the trackball.  Now all I get is a very generic window.  I have 3 buttons, but now only show a choice for 2 in the mouse window and there's nothing for the scroll feature.  Now, when I scroll, the window goes from the very top to the very bottom.  I could control this with my trackball window.<P>Any suggestions other than buying a new trackball??||||reg||5
Z||000001||btoth||09-24-2000||02:14 PM||||i would try to look for some downloadable drivers from the company website that makes your trackball.<P>you could also try unplugging the trackball (if it's not built into the keyboard?) and starting up without it, then tun it off and plug it back in and see if windows recognizes that it's there.<P>just some sugestions.<P>~ brian.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-24-2000||02:16 PM||||Find the website for the company that made your trac-ball and see if they have an updated driver for it. Might could try the Microsoft scrolling middle button mouse driver and see if it works. But then again, I'd just go back to Win98 and be happy again- this coming from a guy who still has Win95 on most everything. Remember, if it aint broke, don't fix it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Loki||09-24-2000||07:28 PM||||Ummm.... Have you re-installed yet?  If not..Then do it...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> WinME is the same thing as Win98, just a little more on the eye candy department. Me personally stay with 98..Thats coming from someone who works at MS<P>Loki||||reg||1
Z||000004||HugGRRRFiero||09-25-2000||08:27 AM||||Do you remember if your trackball came with a 3.5" floppy disk?  Probably it's still in the box it came in.  Try re-installing the drivers again if you've got the disk or download them from their website.<P>I wish my Fiero was more like a computer...  I could solve all my car problems just by re-installing the driver  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">        <BR>        <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000005||Monkeyman||09-25-2000||06:44 PM||||I shut the computer off, then restarted it.  That seemed to fix the problem.  I don't know why since I had to restart my computer a couple of times during the installation.  Thanx everyone for replying so quickly. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-25-2000||09:26 PM||||shuting it off would reinitialize the trackball itself. That's not uncommon with multi emulation mice. (It pretends it's a MS mouse or a logitec or mouse systems mouse depending on what drivers it's used with. Many don't switch modes untill they are shut off)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||09-26-2000||05:19 AM||||Thanx, Ogre.  Shows what I know.  I thought that any external hardware (scanner, mouse, printer, etc) would always present itself to the computer as what it was.  I didn't know that I could pretend to be something else.  I really need to take some computer classes.  I guess I ask some pretty dumb questions when it comes to stuff like this. <P>Be prepared for some more dumb questions in about a week.  I bought a slightly used laptop (ad said "notebooK"---same difference?) off of priceline the other day.  If it doesn't have MS Excel, I'll need to install it and I'm (obviously) clueless. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||09-26-2000||08:51 AM||||I wouldnt worry about taking classes...just keep asking questions.  As for installing Excel, Microsoft makes there installation programs pretty good nowadays.  Just put the CD in the drive and you will get a message that goes something like:  <P><B><I>You have inserted the Microsoft Excel CD.  Excel is not currently installed on this computer.  Your computer will be assimilated.  Surrender your keyboard and mouse.  Lotus will be uninstalled.  Resistance is futile."</B></I><P>It may not be quite that blunt, but nowadays, just pop the CD in the drive (depending on the age of the laptop) and the autorun will kick in and all you have to do is click OK.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
